scription":null,"topics":[],"score":229479,"global_rank":113687,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19713},{"name":"davidbmar/Palindrome-Index","owner":"davidbmar","html_url":"https://github.com/davidbmar/Palindrome-Index","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Given a string, , of lowercase letters, determine the index of the character whose removal will make  a palindrome. If  is already a palindrome or no such character exists, then print . There will always be a valid solution, and any correct answer is acceptable. For example, if  \"bcbc\", we can either remove 'b' at index  or 'c' at index .  Input Format  The first line contains an integer, , denoting the number of test cases.  Each line  of the  subsequent lines (where ) describes a test case in the form of a single string, .  Constraints  All characters are lowercase English letters. Output Format  Print an integer denoting the zero-indexed position of the character that makes  not a palindrome; if  is already a palindrome or no such character exists, print .  Sample Input  3 aaab baa aaa Sample Output  3 0 -1 Explanation  Test Case 1: \"aaab\"  Removing 'b' at index  results in a palindrome, so we print  on a new line.  Test Case 2: \"baa\"  Removing 'b' at index  results in a palindrome, so we print  on a new line.  Test Case 3: \"aaa\"  This string is already a palindrome, so we print ; however, , , and  are also all acceptable answers, as the string will still be a palindrome if any one of the characters at those indices are removed.","topics":[],"score":229466,"global_rank":113703,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19714},{"name":"nonabelian/leapy","owner":"nonabelian","html_url":"https://github.com/nonabelian/leapy","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"BETA: Real-time inference from scalable machine learning in Python","topics":["dask","dask-ml","data-science","inference","machine-learning","pipeli